THIRD-PARTY COMPATIBILITY & INTEROPERABILITY NOTICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. SCOPE OF LICENSE
   The MIT License above applies exclusively to original contributions,
   architecture, bytecode transformers, runtime adapters, stub implementations,
   and integration code authored by the Pryzma project contributors.

2. INTEROPERABILITY & REVERSE ENGINEERING
   Pryzma is an independent compatibility engine designed to restore and
   maintain visual shaderpack and resourcepack functionality within modern
   modding runtimes.

   Portions of compatibility interfaces, format specifications, and runtime
   adapters are developed and included strictly for the purpose of technical
   interoperability, in accordance with recognized statutory reverse engineering
   and interoperability provisions, including:
   - United States Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 107 - Fair Use for Interoperability;
     Sega Enterprises Ltd. v. Accolade, Inc.; Sony Computer Entertainment, Inc. v.
     Connectix Corp.);
   - European Union Directive 2009/24/EC, Article 6 (Decompilation for Interoperability);
   - Civil Code of the Russian Federation, Part IV, Article 1280 (Right of Legitimate
     Users to Decompile and Adapt for Interoperability).

3. NO CLAIM TO PREDECESSOR INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
   The contributors claim no copyright or proprietary ownership in underlying
   third-party shaderpack standards, legacy resource pack formats, or external
   game assets. All trademarks, format identifiers, and intellectual property
   belong to their respective rights holders.

4. NON-AFFILIATION
   Pryzma is an independent community open-source project and is not affiliated
   with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Mojang Studios, Microsoft Corporation,
   or the developers of predecessor visual modifications.

5. RIGHTS HOLDER CONTACT & GOOD FAITH RESOLUTION
   In the event that any copyright holder identifies material in this repository
   that they believe infringes upon their rights, they are encouraged to contact
